 In the dense, humid jungle of Stranglethorn Vale, a small but determined Gnome Warlock named Fizzlewick trudged through the underbrush, his Succubus, Lila, by his side. Lila's crimson skin and provocative attire contrasted sharply with the lush greenery around them. Fizzlewick was on a quest to retrieve a rare orchid for his latest potion. As they ventured deeper, they stumbled upon a group of hostile Naga. Lila lashed out with her whip, striking one of the serpentine humanoids with a bolt of shadow energy. Fizzlewick began to cast his spells, but the Naga were relentless. Just as they were about to be overwhelmed, Lila used her Seduction ability, charming one of the Naga and turning it against its allies. With the tide turned, Fizzlewick and Lila emerged victorious. They found the orchid and made their way back to the safety of Booty Bay, their bond strengthened by the trials of Stranglethorn Vale.

Answer: Most Warlocks are seen with Voidwalkers because they provide better survivability through tanking and threat generation (Torment, Sacrifice, Suffering), making them ideal for the frequent and sometimes unexpected pulls while leveling. Succubus, while offering good single-target damage and crowd control, doesn't provide the same level of safety and durability as a Voidwalker. [end of text]


